    "result_text": "The pipeline is coherent and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) are now consolidated into a single `identityKey`-based check, and `identityKey` is returned on the owner response.\n\n**New `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`** \u2014 a create is rejected with **409** only when a new owner's *whole* key equals an existing owner's.\n\n### New files\n- `model/IdentityKey.java` \u2014 derives the key from an `Owner` (same style as the existing `Locality`/`ContactPreference`/`MembershipLevel` helpers). The owner's stored telephone is already E.164-normalized and email already lower-cased by `ValidateOwnerFields`, so those stored values are the normalized forms; null email/householdId contribute empty segments.\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java` \u2014 the single duplicate-detection step; compares the built owner's key against every existing owner.\n- `rest/escalation/OwnerIdentityConflictException.java` + handler (409) + its escalation YAML.\n\n### Modified\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 removed the `checkTelephone`/`checkEmail`/`checkHousehold` steps; added `checkIdentity` **after `assignHousehold`** so the assigned `householdId` is part of the key (and before `save`, so a duplicate is a 409, not a persisted record).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `identityKey` onto `OwnerDto`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema (regenerates the DTO).\n- `AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 dropped a now-stale javadoc `{@link}` to the deleted household check. (The household *grouping* logic is unchanged \u2014 only duplicate *rejection* moved to the key.)\n\n### Removed\nThe three old check classes and their exception/handler/escalation-YAML trios.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause telephone is now part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones have different keys and are **both allowed** \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` case, which asserts a same-telephone create returns 409).",
